  india_suit_recovery_cpc_37: `You are drafting a filing-grade commercial Summary Suit for Recovery under Order XXXVII of the Code of Civil Procedure, 1908.

Use this mandatory filing-set order: cause title and filing particulars; memo of parties; synopsis and list of dates; commercial-dispute and Order XXXVII maintainability; territorial and pecuniary jurisdiction; limitation; valuation and court fee; Commercial Courts Act §12A compliance or a fact-supported urgent-interim-relief exception; numbered material facts; cause of action; invoice-wise principal/credit/interest schedule; grounds; relief including principal, pre-suit interest, pendente lite and future interest; verification; prescribed Commercial Court Statement of Truth; supporting affidavit; index and list of annexures.

The Order XXXVII averment must identify the written contract, invoices, written acknowledgment, negotiable instrument, guarantee, or other qualifying written debt actually supplied in the facts. Do not assume summary procedure applies to an unliquidated or oral claim. State that no relief outside Order XXXVII is claimed only if that is true from the requested relief.

Use every supplied party name, amount, payment/credit, invoice number, date, due date, notice date, interest rate and forum exactly. Reconcile the invoice schedule arithmetically: invoice principal minus admitted payments/credits plus only supported pre-suit interest must equal the pleaded valuation and principal/interest prayer. Never invent an appropriation, due date, contractual interest rate, court, territorial nexus, mediation event, urgency, court-fee amount, annexure, or monetary total. If a required particular is absent or a calculation cannot be performed from supplied facts, retain a descriptive [BLANK: …] and state what must be confirmed; do not estimate.

Section 12A: plead completion only when mediation filing and outcome/non-starter facts are supplied. Plead the urgent-relief exception only when concrete urgency facts and urgent interim relief are supplied. Otherwise use [BLANK: pre-institution mediation status / urgent-relief basis] and flag it for filing review.

Court fee is ad valorem under the applicable State court-fees legislation/schedule. Do not use a national percentage estimate. State the valuation exactly if supplied and leave [BLANK: state-specific court fee after registry/schedule verification] if the applicable state schedule and computation are not supplied.

Annexures must be indexed actual documents supported by the intake: written contract/purchase order, invoices, delivery/acceptance proof, ledger/account statement, payment/part-payment proof, acknowledgment, demand notice and service proof, Section 12A mediation papers, and corporate authorisation as applicable. Omit unsupported documents rather than inventing them.`,
