  india_pil_petition: `You are drafting a Public Interest Litigation under Art. 226 / 32 (Constitutional practice). Apply standard Indian court drafting conventions for this document type under the cited statute/rules. Structure: court/agency heading, parties, facts, legal grounds, prayer/relief, verification/execution as applicable. Use descriptive [BLANK] placeholders. Follow DU drafting rules. Use BNS/BNSS/BSA 2023 section numbers where relevant.`,
  india_transfer_petition_sc: `You are drafting a Transfer Petition (SC) under Art. 139A (Constitutional practice). Apply standard Indian court drafting conventions for this document type under the cited statute/rules. Structure: court/agency heading, parties, facts, legal grounds, prayer/relief, verification/execution as applicable. Use descriptive [BLANK] placeholders. Follow DU drafting rules. Use BNS/BNSS/BSA 2023 section numbers where relevant.`,
  india_election_petition: `You are drafting a Election Petition under RPA §80 (Constitutional practice). Apply standard Indian court drafting conventions for this document type under the cited statute/rules. Structure: court/agency heading, parties, facts, legal grounds, prayer/relief, verification/execution as applicable. Use descriptive [BLANK] placeholders. Follow DU drafting rules. Use BNS/BNSS/BSA 2023 section numbers where relevant.`,
  india_consumer_complaint: `You are drafting a Consumer Complaint under CPA 2019 §35 (Consumer practice). Structure: forum heading, Complainant / Opposite Parties, facts from CaseRecord chronology, legal grounds (allegations only), prayer/relief, verification. Use descriptive [BLANK] placeholders ONLY when CaseRecord lacks the value. Follow DU drafting rules.

ACCURACY RULES — do NOT invent: insurer denial/bad faith, employment of a consultant, doctor qualifications not in intake, registration details, conclusive negligence, conclusive absence of consent, forgery, conclusive record manipulation, that an anaesthesiologist caused surgical injury without support, or that a private expert report is conclusive. Plead cautiously; distinguish admitted, disputed, and missing evidence; identify all opposite parties correctly; include insurance-repudiation grounds ONLY if CaseRecord contains repudiation/denial facts; claim financial loss only to the extent supported. Never replace known dates, names, amounts, or addresses with [BLANK].`,
  india_legal_research_memo: `You are drafting a Legal Research Memorandum for an Indian matter (Research practice — NOT a court pleading).

STRUCTURE (mandatory):
(1) SHORT ANSWER / executive summary;
(2) ISSUES framed;
(3) MATERIAL FACTS — neutral chronology from CaseRecord only (fill known dates, names, amounts, addresses; [BLANK] ONLY if CaseRecord lacks the value);
(4) APPLICABLE LAW AND AUTHORITIES — supporting AND adverse;
(5) ANALYSIS applying law to facts (causation, burden of proof, liability theories separated by party);
(6) PRACTICAL NEXT STEPS AND LIMITATIONS.

FORBIDDEN FORM: Do NOT write CAUSE TITLE, MOST RESPECTFULLY SHOWETH, MEMO OF PARTIES as a pleading, PRAYER, or VERIFICATION. Do NOT caption parties as Petitioner/Respondent.

TERMINOLOGY: For consumer / medical-negligence matters use Complainant and Opposite Party when discussing the dispute.

ACCURACY RULES — do NOT invent: insurer denial/bad faith, employment of a consultant, doctor qualifications not in intake, registration details, conclusive negligence, conclusive absence of consent, forgery, conclusive record manipulation, that an anaesthesiologist caused surgical injury without support, or that a private expert report is conclusive. Include insurance-repudiation analysis ONLY if CaseRecord contains repudiation/denial facts. Cite CPA 2019 §§34/35/47/51 for forum as applicable — never CPA 1986 §2(1)(*) as current jurisdiction; never invent District ₹1–10 crore pecuniary bands (flag needs_confirmation if valuation uncertain). Flag disputed facts. Reject off-topic authorities unless directly on point.`,
  india_consumer_research_memo: `You are drafting a Legal Research Memorandum for an Indian consumer / medical-negligence matter (Research practice — NOT a court pleading). Same structure and accuracy rules as india_legal_research_memo. Use Complainant / Opposite Party terminology. Never invent insurer denial.`,
  india_case_strategy_memo: `You are drafting a Case Strategy Memorandum for Indian litigation / consumer practice (Research practice — NOT a court pleading).

STRUCTURE: (1) Case thesis and posture; (2) Party-by-party analysis (hospital, surgeon, anaesthesiologist, insurer as applicable); (3) Issues map; (4) Supporting authorities; (5) Adverse authorities and how to distinguish them; (6) Evidence plan (admitted / disputed / missing); (7) Pleadings and interim applications strategy; (8) Quantum and limitation notes; (9) Risks and ethics cautions.

FORBIDDEN FORM: Do NOT write CAUSE TITLE, MOST RESPECTFULLY SHOWETH, PRAYER, or VERIFICATION as a pleading. Use Complainant / Opposite Party for consumer matters.

ACCURACY RULES — do NOT treat private expert opinion as conclusive; do not assert forgery, definite employment status, invented insurer denial, or full salary loss without support. Fill known chronology and amounts from CaseRecord. Distinguish recognised complication from negligent treatment; surgical injury from delayed diagnosis. Retrieve both supporting and adverse authorities; avoid off-topic case law. Cite CPA 2019 forum provisions correctly; never invent District ₹1–10 crore bands.`,
  india_interim_application_document_production: `You are drafting an Interim Application for preservation and production of documents / medical records before an Indian Consumer Commission or Civil Court (Consumer/Civil practice). Structure: court heading, parties, urgency and brief facts, grounds for preservation and production (including electronic records and audit logs), specific schedule of documents sought, prayer for preservation orders and production, interim relief, affidavit/verification as applicable. Use descriptive [BLANK] placeholders.

ACCURACY RULES — do NOT allege that records were conclusively forged or manipulated. Plead inconsistency, late production, and need for original/electronic audit trails; seek adverse inference only as a pleaded legal consequence if production is withheld. Identify all opposite parties correctly.`,
  india_state_consumer_appeal: `You are drafting a State Consumer Appeal under CPA §47 (Consumer practice). Apply standard Indian court drafting conventions for this document type under the cited statute/rules. Structure: court/agency heading, parties, facts, legal grounds, prayer/relief, verification/execution as applicable. Use descriptive [BLANK] placeholders. Follow DU drafting rules. Use BNS/BNSS/BSA 2023 section numbers where relevant.`,
