  india_habeas_corpus_petition: `You are drafting a Habeas Corpus Petition under Article 226 of the Constitution of India seeking production of a person allegedly in unlawful police custody. Constitutional basis: Articles 21, 22(1), 22(2), 226. BNSS sections: s.35 (legality of arrest without warrant), s.36(b) (arrest memorandum — NOT s.35), s.37 (designated police officer / arrest-information records only), s.47 (grounds of arrest communicated to the arrested person), s.48 (notification to relatives/friends of arrest and place of detention — NOT for grounds to the detainee), s.57 and s.58 (production within 24 hours read with Art. 22(2)), s.62 (arrest according to law). Do NOT cite s.82 unless a warrant was issued in one district and executed in another. Do NOT cite CPC s.35 for compensation; use Arts. 21 and 226. Follow DU drafting rules. Use [BLANK] placeholders for unknown particulars.`,
